window.MOCK_BANK=(window.MOCK_BANK||[]).concat([{"id":"v2-71-0230","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Where are we now?","why":"The decisive clue matches Where are we now?: The improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline. Where do we want to be? instead refers to the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets. Did we get there? instead refers to the improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target.","whyNl":"Eerst vaststellen hoe het nu werkt en presteert. Die nulmeting maakt latere vergelijking mogelijk. Een gewenste doelwaarde vastleggen hoort bij de volgende stap, niet bij de baseline. Vergelijk vooral met Where do we want to be?: Hier maak je de gewenste situatie concreet en meetbaar. Twee dagen doorlooptijd als doel is nog geen plan om die waarde te bereiken. Dat plan hoort bij How do we get there.","hook":"Now = baseline.","prompt":"Which statement about the improvement step 'Where are we now' is CORRECT?","options":["The improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline.","The improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets.","The improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target.","The improvement-model step that links improvement to the organization's direction and objectives."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0231","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Where do we want to be?","why":"The decisive clue matches Where do we want to be?: The improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets. Where are we now? instead refers to the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline. How do we get there? instead refers to the improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target.","whyNl":"Hier maak je de gewenste situatie concreet en meetbaar. Twee dagen doorlooptijd als doel is nog geen plan om die waarde te bereiken. Dat plan hoort bij How do we get there. Vergelijk vooral met Where are we now?: Eerst vaststellen hoe het nu werkt en presteert. Die nulmeting maakt latere vergelijking mogelijk. Een gewenste doelwaarde vastleggen hoort bij de volgende stap, niet bij de baseline.","hook":"Destination and measurable target.","prompt":"Which statement about the improvement step 'Where do we want to be' is CORRECT?","options":["The improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets.","The improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline.","The improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target.","The improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0232","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"How do we get there?","why":"The decisive clue matches How do we get there?: The improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target. Where do we want to be? instead refers to the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets. Take action instead refers to the improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed.","whyNl":"Hier bepaal je de aanpak, acties, resources en volgorde. Het gewenste doel ligt al vast; je kiest nu de route. De acties daadwerkelijk uitvoeren hoort bij Take action. Vergelijk vooral met Where do we want to be?: Hier maak je de gewenste situatie concreet en meetbaar. Twee dagen doorlooptijd als doel is nog geen plan om die waarde te bereiken. Dat plan hoort bij How do we get there.","hook":"How = plan the route.","prompt":"Which statement about the improvement step 'How do we get there' is CORRECT?","options":["The improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target.","The improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets.","The improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed.","The improvement-model step that links improvement to the organization's direction and objectives."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0233","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Take action","why":"The decisive clue matches Take action: The improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed. How do we get there? instead refers to the improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target. Did we get there? instead refers to the improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target.","whyNl":"Take action is uitvoering van de afgesproken verbetering. Een plan of doel opschrijven is nog geen uitvoering. Na actie moet je nog beoordelen of de gewenste verbetering echt is bereikt. Vergelijk vooral met How do we get there?: Hier bepaal je de aanpak, acties, resources en volgorde. Het gewenste doel ligt al vast; je kiest nu de route. De acties daadwerkelijk uitvoeren hoort bij Take action.","hook":"Act = do the planned work.","prompt":"Which statement about Take action is CORRECT?","options":["The improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed.","The improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target.","The improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target.","The improvement-model step that embeds learning and sustains further improvement."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0234","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Did we get there?","why":"The decisive clue matches Did we get there?: The improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target. Where are we now? instead refers to the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline. Take action instead refers to the improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed.","whyNl":"Meet en evalueer het effect tegenover het vooraf gekozen doel. Dat er iets is opgeleverd betekent niet automatisch dat het resultaat is gehaald. Vergelijk met doel en baseline, niet alleen met verrichte activiteiten. Vergelijk vooral met Where are we now?: Eerst vaststellen hoe het nu werkt en presteert. Die nulmeting maakt latere vergelijking mogelijk. Een gewenste doelwaarde vastleggen hoort bij de volgende stap, niet bij de baseline.","hook":"Did = evaluate against the target.","prompt":"Which statement about the improvement step 'Did we get there' is CORRECT?","options":["The improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target.","The improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline.","The improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed.","The improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0235","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"How do we keep the momentum going?","why":"The decisive clue matches How do we keep the momentum going?: The improvement-model step that embeds learning and sustains further improvement. Did we get there? instead refers to the improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target. What is the vision? instead refers to the improvement-model step that links improvement to the organization's direction and objectives.","whyNl":"Borg succesvolle werkwijzen, deel wat geleerd is en zoek verdere verbeteringen. Dit gebeurt ook wanneer niet alles is gelukt: gebruik die lessen. Het model eindigt niet bij één afgerond project. Vergelijk vooral met Did we get there?: Meet en evalueer het effect tegenover het vooraf gekozen doel. Dat er iets is opgeleverd betekent niet automatisch dat het resultaat is gehaald. Vergelijk met doel en baseline, niet alleen met verrichte activiteiten.","hook":"Embed learning and keep improving.","prompt":"Which statement about the improvement step 'How do we keep the momentum going' is CORRECT?","options":["The improvement-model step that embeds learning and sustains further improvement.","The improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target.","The improvement-model step that links improvement to the organization's direction and objectives.","The improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0236","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement register","why":"The decisive clue matches Continual improvement register: A place to record, assess and prioritize improvement ideas. Service level agreement instead refers to a documented provider-customer agreement identifying required services and expected service levels. Change instead refers to an addition, modification or removal that can affect services directly or indirectly.","whyNl":"Een improvement register maakt ideeën zichtbaar en helpt beoordelen en prioriteren. Een vermelding is geen automatische toestemming om de verbetering uit te voeren. Meerdere registers kunnen zinvol zijn als ze passend beheerd worden. Vergelijk vooral met Service level agreement: Een SLA legt afspraken over services en servicelevels vast. Goede doelen zijn begrijpelijk en relevant voor de business. De overeenkomst vervangt geen gesprekken over ervaring en zegt niet dat elk individueel componentcijfer een compleet servicebeeld geeft.","hook":"Record an idea; then assess and prioritize.","prompt":"Which statement about Continual improvement register is CORRECT?","options":["A place to record, assess and prioritize improvement ideas.","A documented provider-customer agreement identifying required services and expected service levels.","An addition, modification or removal that can affect services directly or indirectly.","A problem that has been analysed and remains unresolved."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0237","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service level agreement","why":"The decisive clue matches Service level agreement: A documented provider-customer agreement identifying required services and expected service levels. Continual improvement register instead refers to a place to record, assess and prioritize improvement ideas. Service request instead refers to a user-initiated request for an agreed, predefined service action within normal service delivery.","whyNl":"Een SLA legt afspraken over services en servicelevels vast. Goede doelen zijn begrijpelijk en relevant voor de business. De overeenkomst vervangt geen gesprekken over ervaring en zegt niet dat elk individueel componentcijfer een compleet servicebeeld geeft. Vergelijk vooral met Continual improvement register: Een improvement register maakt ideeën zichtbaar en helpt beoordelen en prioriteren. Een vermelding is geen automatische toestemming om de verbetering uit te voeren. Meerdere registers kunnen zinvol zijn als ze passend beheerd worden.","hook":"Agree meaningful service levels.","prompt":"Which statement about Service level agreement is CORRECT?","options":["A documented provider-customer agreement identifying required services and expected service levels.","A place to record, assess and prioritize improvement ideas.","A user-initiated request for an agreed, predefined service action within normal service delivery.","A formal description of one or more services aimed at the needs of a particular consumer group."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0239","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement","why":"The decisive clue matches Continual improvement: Keeping services and practices aligned with changing business needs through ongoing improvement. Service level management instead refers to setting business-based service targets and assessing and managing delivery against them. Change enablement instead refers to increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","whyNl":"Continual improvement brengt diensten en werkwijzen steeds in lijn met veranderende behoeften. Het is geen eenmalig groot project en niet alleen de taak van één manager. Verbeteringen kunnen klein zijn en op elk niveau ontstaan. Vergelijk vooral met Service level management: Service level management maakt bedrijfsgerichte doelen en bewaakt levering daartegen. Alleen technische componentmetingen zijn geen volledig beeld. Gesprekken met klanten en gebruikers helpen om prestaties en ervaring te begrijpen.","hook":"Keep alignment as needs change.","prompt":"In an ITIL 4 context, which statement about Continual improvement is CORRECT?","options":["Keeping services and practices aligned with changing business needs through ongoing improvement.","Setting business-based service targets and assessing and managing delivery against them.","Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","Reducing incident likelihood and impact by managing causes, workarounds and known errors."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0241","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change enablement","why":"The decisive clue matches Change enablement: Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule. Deployment management instead refers to moving new or changed components into live, test or staging environments. Release management instead refers to making new or changed services and features available for use.","whyNl":"Change enablement helpt changes succesvol te laten verlopen met passende risicoafweging, autorisatie en planning. Het doel is niet alle changes blokkeren. De juiste authority hangt af van type en risico. Vergelijk vooral met Deployment management: Deployment is het verplaatsen van componenten naar een omgeving. Het kan om software, hardware of documentatie gaan, en niet uitsluitend productie. Beschikbaar stellen voor gebruik is release management.","hook":"Assess risk, authorize, coordinate.","prompt":"In an ITIL 4 context, which statement about Change enablement is CORRECT?","options":["Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","Moving new or changed components into live, test or staging environments.","Making new or changed services and features available for use.","Keeping services and practices aligned with changing business needs through ongoing improvement."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0243","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident management","why":"The decisive clue matches Incident management: Reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible. Problem management instead refers to reducing incident likelihood and impact by managing causes, workarounds and known errors. Service request management instead refers to handling predefined, user-initiated requests effectively and in a user-friendly way as part of normal service delivery.","whyNl":"Incident management richt zich op herstel. Het mag een workaround gebruiken zonder eerst de definitieve oorzaak weg te nemen. Oorzaakanalyse en structurele beheersing horen primair bij problem management. Vergelijk vooral met Problem management: Problem management onderzoekt oorzaken en mogelijke oorzaken. Het kan proactief zijn en beheert ook workarounds en known errors. Niet ieder problem hoeft meteen definitief opgelost: kosten en baten tellen mee.","hook":"Restore service quickly.","prompt":"In an ITIL 4 context, which statement about Incident management is CORRECT?","options":["Reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible.","Reducing incident likelihood and impact by managing causes, workarounds and known errors.","Handling predefined, user-initiated requests effectively and in a user-friendly way as part of normal service delivery.","Observing services and components and recording and reporting selected meaningful state changes."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0245","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Problem management","why":"The decisive clue matches Problem management: Reducing incident likelihood and impact by managing causes, workarounds and known errors. Incident management instead refers to reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible. Monitoring and event management instead refers to observing services and components and recording and reporting selected meaningful state changes.","whyNl":"Problem management onderzoekt oorzaken en mogelijke oorzaken. Het kan proactief zijn en beheert ook workarounds en known errors. Niet ieder problem hoeft meteen definitief opgelost: kosten en baten tellen mee. Vergelijk vooral met Incident management: Incident management richt zich op herstel. Het mag een workaround gebruiken zonder eerst de definitieve oorzaak weg te nemen. Oorzaakanalyse en structurele beheersing horen primair bij problem management.","hook":"Causes, workarounds and known errors.","prompt":"In an ITIL 4 context, which statement about Problem management is CORRECT?","options":["Reducing incident likelihood and impact by managing causes, workarounds and known errors.","Reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible.","Observing services and components and recording and reporting selected meaningful state changes.","Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0247","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service request management","why":"The decisive clue matches Service request management: Handling predefined, user-initiated requests effectively and in a user-friendly way as part of normal service delivery. Incident management instead refers to reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible. Change enablement instead refers to increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","whyNl":"Service requests zijn vooraf gedefinieerde gebruikersverzoeken die bij normale dienstverlening horen. Dat maakt ze vaak voorspelbaar. Goedkeuring kan nog nodig zijn, ook als het verzoek routine is. Vergelijk vooral met Incident management: Incident management richt zich op herstel. Het mag een workaround gebruiken zonder eerst de definitieve oorzaak weg te nemen. Oorzaakanalyse en structurele beheersing horen primair bij problem management.","hook":"Normal, predefined user requests.","prompt":"In an ITIL 4 context, which statement about Service request management is CORRECT?","options":["Handling predefined, user-initiated requests effectively and in a user-friendly way as part of normal service delivery.","Reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible.","Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","Capturing demand for incident resolution and requests and acting as the users' entry point to the service provider."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0249","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service desk","why":"The decisive clue matches Service desk: Capturing demand for incident resolution and requests and acting as the users' entry point to the service provider. Service request management instead refers to handling predefined, user-initiated requests effectively and in a user-friendly way as part of normal service delivery. Relationship management instead refers to building and maintaining links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels.","whyNl":"De service desk is de ingang en het centrale contactpunt voor gebruikers. Hij hoeft niet elk technisch probleem zelf op te lossen. Begrip, empathie en communicatie blijven belangrijk, ook met automatisering. Vergelijk vooral met Service request management: Service requests zijn vooraf gedefinieerde gebruikersverzoeken die bij normale dienstverlening horen. Dat maakt ze vaak voorspelbaar. Goedkeuring kan nog nodig zijn, ook als het verzoek routine is.","hook":"Single point of contact for users.","prompt":"In an ITIL 4 context, which statement about Service desk is CORRECT?","options":["Capturing demand for incident resolution and requests and acting as the users' entry point to the service provider.","Handling predefined, user-initiated requests effectively and in a user-friendly way as part of normal service delivery.","Building and maintaining links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels.","Reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0251","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service level management","why":"The decisive clue matches Service level management: Setting business-based service targets and assessing and managing delivery against them. Relationship management instead refers to building and maintaining links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels. Monitoring and event management instead refers to observing services and components and recording and reporting selected meaningful state changes.","whyNl":"Service level management maakt bedrijfsgerichte doelen en bewaakt levering daartegen. Alleen technische componentmetingen zijn geen volledig beeld. Gesprekken met klanten en gebruikers helpen om prestaties en ervaring te begrijpen. Vergelijk vooral met Relationship management: Relationship management onderhoudt relaties en begrip op strategisch en tactisch niveau. Supplier management richt zich specifiek op leveranciers en hun prestaties. De service desk is vooral het contactpunt met gebruikers voor operationele vragen.","hook":"Business-based targets, not just green dashboards.","prompt":"In an ITIL 4 context, which statement about Service level management is CORRECT?","options":["Setting business-based service targets and assessing and managing delivery against them.","Building and maintaining links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels.","Observing services and components and recording and reporting selected meaningful state changes.","Managing suppliers and their performance so they support quality service provision."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0252","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service request","why":"The decisive clue matches Service request: A user-initiated request for an agreed, predefined service action within normal service delivery. Incident instead refers to an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality. Problem instead refers to a cause or possible cause of one or more incidents.","whyNl":"Een service request vraagt om een afgesproken standaardactie, bijvoorbeeld toegang of informatie. Dat verschilt van onverwachte uitval. Een verzoek kan nog steeds autorisatie nodig hebben en kan via een standard change worden afgehandeld. Vergelijk vooral met Incident: Een incident hoeft geen volledige uitval te zijn. Een onverwachte kwaliteitsvermindering, zoals ernstige vertraging, kan ook een incident zijn. De oorzaak van de verstoring is een problem; dat is een ander begrip.","hook":"Request = ask for a normal service action.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Service request?","options":["A user asks for access to an application using an agreed catalogue item. No service has failed.","A normally fast application unexpectedly becomes too slow to meet service needs, although it is still running.","Engineers identify a defect that could interrupt transactions in future, even though no interruption has occurred yet.","A monitor records that a scheduled backup has completed successfully."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0253","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Workaround","why":"The decisive clue matches Workaround: A way to reduce or remove impact while a complete resolution is not available. Standard change instead refers to a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place. Known error instead refers to a problem that has been analysed and remains unresolved.","whyNl":"Een workaround beperkt impact wanneer de volledige oplossing ontbreekt. Hij kan een incident herstellen terwijl het onderliggende problem open blijft. Het is geen bewijs dat de definitieve oorzaak is weggenomen. Vergelijk vooral met Standard change: Een standard change is vooraf geautoriseerd, laag risico, goed begrepen en gedocumenteerd. Klein of vaak uitgevoerd zijn is op zichzelf onvoldoende. Als de procedure verandert, moet die wijziging opnieuw passend beoordeeld worden.","hook":"Temporary impact reduction, not necessarily a permanent fix.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Workaround?","options":["Switching to a spare printer lets staff work while the failed component awaits replacement.","A low-risk account setup follows an approved, documented and well-understood procedure with no additional change authorization required.","A problem investigation is complete, but the problem has not been resolved and no workable workaround exists.","Engineers identify a defect that could interrupt transactions in future, even though no interruption has occurred yet."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0254","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Standard change","why":"The decisive clue matches Standard change: A low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place. Normal change instead refers to a change requiring scheduling, assessment and authorization through the appropriate process. Emergency change instead refers to a change needing implementation as soon as possible, with expedited assessment and authorization.","whyNl":"Een standard change is vooraf geautoriseerd, laag risico, goed begrepen en gedocumenteerd. Klein of vaak uitgevoerd zijn is op zichzelf onvoldoende. Als de procedure verandert, moet die wijziging opnieuw passend beoordeeld worden. Vergelijk vooral met Normal change: Een normal change moet gepland, beoordeeld en geautoriseerd worden. Hij hoeft niet groot of risicovol te zijn. Het ontbreken van voorafgaande autorisatie onderscheidt hem van een standard change.","hook":"Standard = pre-authorized procedure.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Standard change?","options":["A low-risk account setup follows an approved, documented and well-understood procedure with no additional change authorization required.","A modest service modification is neither urgent nor covered by a pre-authorized procedure. It needs assessment and authorization.","A serious newly discovered vulnerability needs a fix as soon as possible through accelerated assessment and authorization.","A user asks for access to an application using an agreed catalogue item. No service has failed."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0255","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Normal change","why":"The decisive clue matches Normal change: A change requiring scheduling, assessment and authorization through the appropriate process. Standard change instead refers to a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place. Emergency change instead refers to a change needing implementation as soon as possible, with expedited assessment and authorization.","whyNl":"Een normal change moet gepland, beoordeeld en geautoriseerd worden. Hij hoeft niet groot of risicovol te zijn. Het ontbreken van voorafgaande autorisatie onderscheidt hem van een standard change. Vergelijk vooral met Standard change: Een standard change is vooraf geautoriseerd, laag risico, goed begrepen en gedocumenteerd. Klein of vaak uitgevoerd zijn is op zichzelf onvoldoende. Als de procedure verandert, moet die wijziging opnieuw passend beoordeeld worden.","hook":"Normal = assess, authorize and schedule.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Normal change?","options":["A modest service modification is neither urgent nor covered by a pre-authorized procedure. It needs assessment and authorization.","A low-risk account setup follows an approved, documented and well-understood procedure with no additional change authorization required.","A serious newly discovered vulnerability needs a fix as soon as possible through accelerated assessment and authorization.","A user asks for access to an application using an agreed catalogue item. No service has failed."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0256","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Emergency change","why":"The decisive clue matches Emergency change: A change needing implementation as soon as possible, with expedited assessment and authorization. Standard change instead refers to a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place. Normal change instead refers to a change requiring scheduling, assessment and authorization through the appropriate process.","whyNl":"Emergency verandert de snelheid van de behandeling, niet de noodzaak van passende controle. Beoordeling en autorisatie worden versneld. Niet elke haastige wens is een emergency change. Vergelijk vooral met Standard change: Een standard change is vooraf geautoriseerd, laag risico, goed begrepen en gedocumenteerd. Klein of vaak uitgevoerd zijn is op zichzelf onvoldoende. Als de procedure verandert, moet die wijziging opnieuw passend beoordeeld worden.","hook":"Expedited control, not no control.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Emergency change?","options":["A serious newly discovered vulnerability needs a fix as soon as possible through accelerated assessment and authorization.","A low-risk account setup follows an approved, documented and well-understood procedure with no additional change authorization required.","A modest service modification is neither urgent nor covered by a pre-authorized procedure. It needs assessment and authorization.","A normally fast application unexpectedly becomes too slow to meet service needs, although it is still running."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0257","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change authority","why":"The decisive clue matches Change authority: The person or group empowered to authorize a change. Sponsor instead refers to the consumer role with authority to approve the budget for consuming a service. Customer instead refers to the consumer role that sets service requirements and takes responsibility for consumption outcomes.","whyNl":"Een change authority is de persoon of groep die bevoegd is een change te autoriseren. Die hoeft niet voor alle changes gelijk te zijn. Een verplichte centrale CAB voor elke change is geen algemene ITIL 4-eis. Vergelijk vooral met Sponsor: De sponsor autoriseert het budget. Die rol hoeft de service niet dagelijks te gebruiken of alle eisen op te stellen. Een manager is dus niet automatisch de customer: budgetvrijgave wijst specifiek op sponsor.","hook":"Authority = the appropriate authorizer.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Change authority?","options":["An organization delegates approval for one change model to a product team and another to a risk committee.","A finance director approves the budget for a hosted recruitment service.","A department head defines what a recruitment service must achieve and accepts responsibility for the hiring outcomes.","Capturing demand for incident resolution and requests and acting as the users' entry point to the service provider."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0258","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"What is the vision?","why":"The decisive clue matches What is the vision?: The improvement-model step that links improvement to the organization's direction and objectives. Where are we now? instead refers to the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline. Where do we want to be? instead refers to the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets.","whyNl":"In deze stap bepaal je waarom de verbetering ertoe doet in het licht van visie, missie en doelen. Een meetbaar specifiek verbeterdoel komt later. Richting kiezen is niet hetzelfde als een stappenplan uitvoeren. Vergelijk vooral met Where are we now?: Eerst vaststellen hoe het nu werkt en presteert. Die nulmeting maakt latere vergelijking mogelijk. Een gewenste doelwaarde vastleggen hoort bij de volgende stap, niet bij de baseline.","hook":"Why improve? Link to the organizational direction.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates the improvement step 'What is the vision'?","options":["Before defining a service improvement, a team clarifies how it supports the organization's mission and strategic goals.","A team measures current waiting times and documents present capabilities before setting a target.","After measuring a six-day turnaround, a team defines success as three days within two months.","The target is agreed. The team now chooses the actions, resources and sequence needed to reach it."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0259","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Where are we now?","why":"The decisive clue matches Where are we now?: The improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline. Where do we want to be? instead refers to the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets. Did we get there? instead refers to the improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target.","whyNl":"Eerst vaststellen hoe het nu werkt en presteert. Die nulmeting maakt latere vergelijking mogelijk. Een gewenste doelwaarde vastleggen hoort bij de volgende stap, niet bij de baseline. Vergelijk vooral met Where do we want to be?: Hier maak je de gewenste situatie concreet en meetbaar. Twee dagen doorlooptijd als doel is nog geen plan om die waarde te bereiken. Dat plan hoort bij How do we get there.","hook":"Now = baseline.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates the improvement step 'Where are we now'?","options":["A team measures current waiting times and documents present capabilities before setting a target.","After measuring a six-day turnaround, a team defines success as three days within two months.","The team compares measured results after a change with its agreed turnaround target.","Before defining a service improvement, a team clarifies how it supports the organization's mission and strategic goals."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0260","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Where do we want to be?","why":"The decisive clue matches Where do we want to be?: The improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets. Where are we now? instead refers to the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline. How do we get there? instead refers to the improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target.","whyNl":"Hier maak je de gewenste situatie concreet en meetbaar. Twee dagen doorlooptijd als doel is nog geen plan om die waarde te bereiken. Dat plan hoort bij How do we get there. Vergelijk vooral met Where are we now?: Eerst vaststellen hoe het nu werkt en presteert. Die nulmeting maakt latere vergelijking mogelijk. Een gewenste doelwaarde vastleggen hoort bij de volgende stap, niet bij de baseline.","hook":"Destination and measurable target.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates the improvement step 'Where do we want to be'?","options":["After measuring a six-day turnaround, a team defines success as three days within two months.","A team measures current waiting times and documents present capabilities before setting a target.","The target is agreed. The team now chooses the actions, resources and sequence needed to reach it.","Staff now implement the workflow changes described in the agreed improvement plan."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0261","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"How do we get there?","why":"The decisive clue matches How do we get there?: The improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target. Where do we want to be? instead refers to the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets. Take action instead refers to the improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed.","whyNl":"Hier bepaal je de aanpak, acties, resources en volgorde. Het gewenste doel ligt al vast; je kiest nu de route. De acties daadwerkelijk uitvoeren hoort bij Take action. Vergelijk vooral met Where do we want to be?: Hier maak je de gewenste situatie concreet en meetbaar. Twee dagen doorlooptijd als doel is nog geen plan om die waarde te bereiken. Dat plan hoort bij How do we get there.","hook":"How = plan the route.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates the improvement step 'How do we get there'?","options":["The target is agreed. The team now chooses the actions, resources and sequence needed to reach it.","After measuring a six-day turnaround, a team defines success as three days within two months.","Staff now implement the workflow changes described in the agreed improvement plan.","Before defining a service improvement, a team clarifies how it supports the organization's mission and strategic goals."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0262","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Take action","why":"The decisive clue matches Take action: The improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed. How do we get there? instead refers to the improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target. Did we get there? instead refers to the improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target.","whyNl":"Take action is uitvoering van de afgesproken verbetering. Een plan of doel opschrijven is nog geen uitvoering. Na actie moet je nog beoordelen of de gewenste verbetering echt is bereikt. Vergelijk vooral met How do we get there?: Hier bepaal je de aanpak, acties, resources en volgorde. Het gewenste doel ligt al vast; je kiest nu de route. De acties daadwerkelijk uitvoeren hoort bij Take action.","hook":"Act = do the planned work.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Take action?","options":["Staff now implement the workflow changes described in the agreed improvement plan.","The target is agreed. The team now chooses the actions, resources and sequence needed to reach it.","The team compares measured results after a change with its agreed turnaround target.","After evaluating results, managers reinforce effective new habits and use lessons to plan further improvement."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0263","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Did we get there?","why":"The decisive clue matches Did we get there?: The improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target. Where are we now? instead refers to the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline. Take action instead refers to the improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed.","whyNl":"Meet en evalueer het effect tegenover het vooraf gekozen doel. Dat er iets is opgeleverd betekent niet automatisch dat het resultaat is gehaald. Vergelijk met doel en baseline, niet alleen met verrichte activiteiten. Vergelijk vooral met Where are we now?: Eerst vaststellen hoe het nu werkt en presteert. Die nulmeting maakt latere vergelijking mogelijk. Een gewenste doelwaarde vastleggen hoort bij de volgende stap, niet bij de baseline.","hook":"Did = evaluate against the target.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates the improvement step 'Did we get there'?","options":["The team compares measured results after a change with its agreed turnaround target.","A team measures current waiting times and documents present capabilities before setting a target.","Staff now implement the workflow changes described in the agreed improvement plan.","After measuring a six-day turnaround, a team defines success as three days within two months."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0264","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"How do we keep the momentum going?","why":"The decisive clue matches How do we keep the momentum going?: The improvement-model step that embeds learning and sustains further improvement. Did we get there? instead refers to the improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target. What is the vision? instead refers to the improvement-model step that links improvement to the organization's direction and objectives.","whyNl":"Borg succesvolle werkwijzen, deel wat geleerd is en zoek verdere verbeteringen. Dit gebeurt ook wanneer niet alles is gelukt: gebruik die lessen. Het model eindigt niet bij één afgerond project. Vergelijk vooral met Did we get there?: Meet en evalueer het effect tegenover het vooraf gekozen doel. Dat er iets is opgeleverd betekent niet automatisch dat het resultaat is gehaald. Vergelijk met doel en baseline, niet alleen met verrichte activiteiten.","hook":"Embed learning and keep improving.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates the improvement step 'How do we keep the momentum going'?","options":["After evaluating results, managers reinforce effective new habits and use lessons to plan further improvement.","The team compares measured results after a change with its agreed turnaround target.","Before defining a service improvement, a team clarifies how it supports the organization's mission and strategic goals.","The target is agreed. The team now chooses the actions, resources and sequence needed to reach it."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0265","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement register","why":"The decisive clue matches Continual improvement register: A place to record, assess and prioritize improvement ideas. Service level agreement instead refers to a documented provider-customer agreement identifying required services and expected service levels. Change instead refers to an addition, modification or removal that can affect services directly or indirectly.","whyNl":"Een improvement register maakt ideeën zichtbaar en helpt beoordelen en prioriteren. Een vermelding is geen automatische toestemming om de verbetering uit te voeren. Meerdere registers kunnen zinvol zijn als ze passend beheerd worden. Vergelijk vooral met Service level agreement: Een SLA legt afspraken over services en servicelevels vast. Goede doelen zijn begrijpelijk en relevant voor de business. De overeenkomst vervangt geen gesprekken over ervaring en zegt niet dat elk individueel componentcijfer een compleet servicebeeld geeft.","hook":"Record an idea; then assess and prioritize.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Continual improvement register?","options":["An employee logs a suggestion so it can be evaluated and prioritized with other improvement opportunities.","A provider and customer document which service is required and the levels at which it should be delivered.","A team removes a routing rule that can indirectly affect how a service operates.","A problem investigation is complete, but the problem has not been resolved and no workable workaround exists."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0266","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service level agreement","why":"The decisive clue matches Service level agreement: A documented provider-customer agreement identifying required services and expected service levels. Continual improvement register instead refers to a place to record, assess and prioritize improvement ideas. Service request instead refers to a user-initiated request for an agreed, predefined service action within normal service delivery.","whyNl":"Een SLA legt afspraken over services en servicelevels vast. Goede doelen zijn begrijpelijk en relevant voor de business. De overeenkomst vervangt geen gesprekken over ervaring en zegt niet dat elk individueel componentcijfer een compleet servicebeeld geeft. Vergelijk vooral met Continual improvement register: Een improvement register maakt ideeën zichtbaar en helpt beoordelen en prioriteren. Een vermelding is geen automatische toestemming om de verbetering uit te voeren. Meerdere registers kunnen zinvol zijn als ze passend beheerd worden.","hook":"Agree meaningful service levels.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Service level agreement?","options":["A provider and customer document which service is required and the levels at which it should be delivered.","An employee logs a suggestion so it can be evaluated and prioritized with other improvement opportunities.","A user asks for access to an application using an agreed catalogue item. No service has failed.","A provider describes a starter package for small charities, combining hosted accounts, a supplied device and onboarding support."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0267","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement","why":"The decisive clue matches Continual improvement: Keeping services and practices aligned with changing business needs through ongoing improvement. Service level management instead refers to setting business-based service targets and assessing and managing delivery against them. Change enablement instead refers to increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","whyNl":"Continual improvement brengt diensten en werkwijzen steeds in lijn met veranderende behoeften. Het is geen eenmalig groot project en niet alleen de taak van één manager. Verbeteringen kunnen klein zijn en op elk niveau ontstaan. Vergelijk vooral met Service level management: Service level management maakt bedrijfsgerichte doelen en bewaakt levering daartegen. Alleen technische componentmetingen zijn geen volledig beeld. Gesprekken met klanten en gebruikers helpen om prestaties en ervaring te begrijpen.","hook":"Keep alignment as needs change.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Continual improvement?","options":["Keeping services and practices aligned with changing business needs through ongoing improvement.","Setting business-based service targets and assessing and managing delivery against them.","Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","Reducing incident likelihood and impact by managing causes, workarounds and known errors."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0268","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change enablement","why":"The decisive clue matches Change enablement: Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule. Deployment management instead refers to moving new or changed components into live, test or staging environments. Release management instead refers to making new or changed services and features available for use.","whyNl":"Change enablement helpt changes succesvol te laten verlopen met passende risicoafweging, autorisatie en planning. Het doel is niet alle changes blokkeren. De juiste authority hangt af van type en risico. Vergelijk vooral met Deployment management: Deployment is het verplaatsen van componenten naar een omgeving. Het kan om software, hardware of documentatie gaan, en niet uitsluitend productie. Beschikbaar stellen voor gebruik is release management.","hook":"Assess risk, authorize, coordinate.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Change enablement?","options":["Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","Moving new or changed components into live, test or staging environments.","Making new or changed services and features available for use.","Keeping services and practices aligned with changing business needs through ongoing improvement."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0269","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident management","why":"The decisive clue matches Incident management: Reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible. Problem management instead refers to reducing incident likelihood and impact by managing causes, workarounds and known errors. Service request management instead refers to handling predefined, user-initiated requests effectively and in a user-friendly way as part of normal service delivery.","whyNl":"Incident management richt zich op herstel. Het mag een workaround gebruiken zonder eerst de definitieve oorzaak weg te nemen. Oorzaakanalyse en structurele beheersing horen primair bij problem management. Vergelijk vooral met Problem management: Problem management onderzoekt oorzaken en mogelijke oorzaken. Het kan proactief zijn en beheert ook workarounds en known errors. Niet ieder problem hoeft meteen definitief opgelost: kosten en baten tellen mee.","hook":"Restore service quickly.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Incident management?","options":["Reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible.","Reducing incident likelihood and impact by managing causes, workarounds and known errors.","Handling predefined, user-initiated requests effectively and in a user-friendly way as part of normal service delivery.","Observing services and components and recording and reporting selected meaningful state changes."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0270","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Problem management","why":"The decisive clue matches Problem management: Reducing incident likelihood and impact by managing causes, workarounds and known errors. Incident management instead refers to reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible. Monitoring and event management instead refers to observing services and components and recording and reporting selected meaningful state changes.","whyNl":"Problem management onderzoekt oorzaken en mogelijke oorzaken. Het kan proactief zijn en beheert ook workarounds en known errors. Niet ieder problem hoeft meteen definitief opgelost: kosten en baten tellen mee. Vergelijk vooral met Incident management: Incident management richt zich op herstel. Het mag een workaround gebruiken zonder eerst de definitieve oorzaak weg te nemen. Oorzaakanalyse en structurele beheersing horen primair bij problem management.","hook":"Causes, workarounds and known errors.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Problem management?","options":["Reducing incident likelihood and impact by managing causes, workarounds and known errors.","Reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible.","Observing services and components and recording and reporting selected meaningful state changes.","Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0271","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service request management","why":"The decisive clue matches Service request management: Handling predefined, user-initiated requests effectively and in a user-friendly way as part of normal service delivery. Incident management instead refers to reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible. Change enablement instead refers to increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","whyNl":"Service requests zijn vooraf gedefinieerde gebruikersverzoeken die bij normale dienstverlening horen. Dat maakt ze vaak voorspelbaar. Goedkeuring kan nog nodig zijn, ook als het verzoek routine is. Vergelijk vooral met Incident management: Incident management richt zich op herstel. Het mag een workaround gebruiken zonder eerst de definitieve oorzaak weg te nemen. Oorzaakanalyse en structurele beheersing horen primair bij problem management.","hook":"Normal, predefined user requests.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Service request management?","options":["Handling predefined, user-initiated requests effectively and in a user-friendly way as part of normal service delivery.","Reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible.","Increasing successful changes through appropriate risk assessment, authorization and management of the change schedule.","Capturing demand for incident resolution and requests and acting as the users' entry point to the service provider."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0272","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service desk","why":"The decisive clue matches Service desk: Capturing demand for incident resolution and requests and acting as the users' entry point to the service provider. Service request management instead refers to handling predefined, user-initiated requests effectively and in a user-friendly way as part of normal service delivery. Relationship management instead refers to building and maintaining links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels.","whyNl":"De service desk is de ingang en het centrale contactpunt voor gebruikers. Hij hoeft niet elk technisch probleem zelf op te lossen. Begrip, empathie en communicatie blijven belangrijk, ook met automatisering. Vergelijk vooral met Service request management: Service requests zijn vooraf gedefinieerde gebruikersverzoeken die bij normale dienstverlening horen. Dat maakt ze vaak voorspelbaar. Goedkeuring kan nog nodig zijn, ook als het verzoek routine is.","hook":"Single point of contact for users.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Service desk?","options":["Capturing demand for incident resolution and requests and acting as the users' entry point to the service provider.","Handling predefined, user-initiated requests effectively and in a user-friendly way as part of normal service delivery.","Building and maintaining links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels.","Reducing incident impact by restoring normal service operation as quickly as possible."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0273","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service level management","why":"The decisive clue matches Service level management: Setting business-based service targets and assessing and managing delivery against them. Relationship management instead refers to building and maintaining links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels. Monitoring and event management instead refers to observing services and components and recording and reporting selected meaningful state changes.","whyNl":"Service level management maakt bedrijfsgerichte doelen en bewaakt levering daartegen. Alleen technische componentmetingen zijn geen volledig beeld. Gesprekken met klanten en gebruikers helpen om prestaties en ervaring te begrijpen. Vergelijk vooral met Relationship management: Relationship management onderhoudt relaties en begrip op strategisch en tactisch niveau. Supplier management richt zich specifiek op leveranciers en hun prestaties. De service desk is vooral het contactpunt met gebruikers voor operationele vragen.","hook":"Business-based targets, not just green dashboards.","prompt":"Which situation MOST clearly illustrates Service level management?","options":["Setting business-based service targets and assessing and managing delivery against them.","Building and maintaining links between an organization and its stakeholders at strategic and tactical levels.","Observing services and components and recording and reporting selected meaningful state changes.","Managing suppliers and their performance so they support quality service provision."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0274","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service request","why":"The decisive clue matches Service request: A user-initiated request for an agreed, predefined service action within normal service delivery. Incident instead refers to an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality. Problem instead refers to a cause or possible cause of one or more incidents.","whyNl":"Een service request vraagt om een afgesproken standaardactie, bijvoorbeeld toegang of informatie. Dat verschilt van onverwachte uitval. Een verzoek kan nog steeds autorisatie nodig hebben en kan via een standard change worden afgehandeld. Vergelijk vooral met Incident: Een incident hoeft geen volledige uitval te zijn. Een onverwachte kwaliteitsvermindering, zoals ernstige vertraging, kan ook een incident zijn. De oorzaak van de verstoring is een problem; dat is een ander begrip.","hook":"Request = ask for a normal service action.","prompt":"Which statement BEST distinguishes Service request from Incident?","options":["Service request is concerned with a user-initiated request for an agreed, predefined service action within normal service delivery.; Incident is concerned with an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality..","Service request is concerned with an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality.; Incident is concerned with a user-initiated request for an agreed, predefined service action within normal service delivery..","Both are primarily concerned with a cause or possible cause of one or more incidents.","Both are primarily concerned with a change of state significant to managing a service or configuration item."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0275","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Workaround","why":"The decisive clue matches Workaround: A way to reduce or remove impact while a complete resolution is not available. Standard change instead refers to a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place. Known error instead refers to a problem that has been analysed and remains unresolved.","whyNl":"Een workaround beperkt impact wanneer de volledige oplossing ontbreekt. Hij kan een incident herstellen terwijl het onderliggende problem open blijft. Het is geen bewijs dat de definitieve oorzaak is weggenomen. Vergelijk vooral met Standard change: Een standard change is vooraf geautoriseerd, laag risico, goed begrepen en gedocumenteerd. Klein of vaak uitgevoerd zijn is op zichzelf onvoldoende. Als de procedure verandert, moet die wijziging opnieuw passend beoordeeld worden.","hook":"Temporary impact reduction, not necessarily a permanent fix.","prompt":"Which statement BEST distinguishes Workaround from Standard change?","options":["Workaround is concerned with a way to reduce or remove impact while a complete resolution is not available.; Standard change is concerned with a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place..","Workaround is concerned with a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place.; Standard change is concerned with a way to reduce or remove impact while a complete resolution is not available..","Both are primarily concerned with a problem that has been analysed and remains unresolved.","Both are primarily concerned with a cause or possible cause of one or more incidents."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0276","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Standard change","why":"The decisive clue matches Standard change: A low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place. Normal change instead refers to a change requiring scheduling, assessment and authorization through the appropriate process. Emergency change instead refers to a change needing implementation as soon as possible, with expedited assessment and authorization.","whyNl":"Een standard change is vooraf geautoriseerd, laag risico, goed begrepen en gedocumenteerd. Klein of vaak uitgevoerd zijn is op zichzelf onvoldoende. Als de procedure verandert, moet die wijziging opnieuw passend beoordeeld worden. Vergelijk vooral met Normal change: Een normal change moet gepland, beoordeeld en geautoriseerd worden. Hij hoeft niet groot of risicovol te zijn. Het ontbreken van voorafgaande autorisatie onderscheidt hem van een standard change.","hook":"Standard = pre-authorized procedure.","prompt":"Which statement BEST distinguishes Standard change from Normal change?","options":["Standard change is concerned with a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place.; Normal change is concerned with a change requiring scheduling, assessment and authorization through the appropriate process..","Standard change is concerned with a change requiring scheduling, assessment and authorization through the appropriate process.; Normal change is concerned with a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place..","Both are primarily concerned with a change needing implementation as soon as possible, with expedited assessment and authorization.","Both are primarily concerned with a user-initiated request for an agreed, predefined service action within normal service delivery."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0277","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Normal change","why":"The decisive clue matches Normal change: A change requiring scheduling, assessment and authorization through the appropriate process. Standard change instead refers to a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place. Emergency change instead refers to a change needing implementation as soon as possible, with expedited assessment and authorization.","whyNl":"Een normal change moet gepland, beoordeeld en geautoriseerd worden. Hij hoeft niet groot of risicovol te zijn. Het ontbreken van voorafgaande autorisatie onderscheidt hem van een standard change. Vergelijk vooral met Standard change: Een standard change is vooraf geautoriseerd, laag risico, goed begrepen en gedocumenteerd. Klein of vaak uitgevoerd zijn is op zichzelf onvoldoende. Als de procedure verandert, moet die wijziging opnieuw passend beoordeeld worden.","hook":"Normal = assess, authorize and schedule.","prompt":"Which statement BEST distinguishes Normal change from Standard change?","options":["Normal change is concerned with a change requiring scheduling, assessment and authorization through the appropriate process.; Standard change is concerned with a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place..","Normal change is concerned with a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place.; Standard change is concerned with a change requiring scheduling, assessment and authorization through the appropriate process..","Both are primarily concerned with a change needing implementation as soon as possible, with expedited assessment and authorization.","Both are primarily concerned with a user-initiated request for an agreed, predefined service action within normal service delivery."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0278","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Emergency change","why":"The decisive clue matches Emergency change: A change needing implementation as soon as possible, with expedited assessment and authorization. Standard change instead refers to a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place. Normal change instead refers to a change requiring scheduling, assessment and authorization through the appropriate process.","whyNl":"Emergency verandert de snelheid van de behandeling, niet de noodzaak van passende controle. Beoordeling en autorisatie worden versneld. Niet elke haastige wens is een emergency change. Vergelijk vooral met Standard change: Een standard change is vooraf geautoriseerd, laag risico, goed begrepen en gedocumenteerd. Klein of vaak uitgevoerd zijn is op zichzelf onvoldoende. Als de procedure verandert, moet die wijziging opnieuw passend beoordeeld worden.","hook":"Expedited control, not no control.","prompt":"Which statement BEST distinguishes Emergency change from Standard change?","options":["Emergency change is concerned with a change needing implementation as soon as possible, with expedited assessment and authorization.; Standard change is concerned with a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place..","Emergency change is concerned with a low-risk, well-understood and documented change with authorization already in place.; Standard change is concerned with a change needing implementation as soon as possible, with expedited assessment and authorization..","Both are primarily concerned with a change requiring scheduling, assessment and authorization through the appropriate process.","Both are primarily concerned with an unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0279","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change authority","why":"The decisive clue matches Change authority: The person or group empowered to authorize a change. Sponsor instead refers to the consumer role with authority to approve the budget for consuming a service. Customer instead refers to the consumer role that sets service requirements and takes responsibility for consumption outcomes.","whyNl":"Een change authority is de persoon of groep die bevoegd is een change te autoriseren. Die hoeft niet voor alle changes gelijk te zijn. Een verplichte centrale CAB voor elke change is geen algemene ITIL 4-eis. Vergelijk vooral met Sponsor: De sponsor autoriseert het budget. Die rol hoeft de service niet dagelijks te gebruiken of alle eisen op te stellen. Een manager is dus niet automatisch de customer: budgetvrijgave wijst specifiek op sponsor.","hook":"Authority = the appropriate authorizer.","prompt":"Which statement BEST distinguishes Change authority from Sponsor?","options":["Change authority is concerned with the person or group empowered to authorize a change.; Sponsor is concerned with the consumer role with authority to approve the budget for consuming a service..","Change authority is concerned with the consumer role with authority to approve the budget for consuming a service.; Sponsor is concerned with the person or group empowered to authorize a change..","Both are primarily concerned with the consumer role that sets service requirements and takes responsibility for consumption outcomes.","Both are primarily concerned with capturing demand for incident resolution and requests and acting as the users' entry point to the service provider."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0280","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"What is the vision?","why":"The decisive clue matches What is the vision?: The improvement-model step that links improvement to the organization's direction and objectives. Where are we now? instead refers to the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline. Where do we want to be? instead refers to the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets.","whyNl":"In deze stap bepaal je waarom de verbetering ertoe doet in het licht van visie, missie en doelen. Een meetbaar specifiek verbeterdoel komt later. Richting kiezen is niet hetzelfde als een stappenplan uitvoeren. Vergelijk vooral met Where are we now?: Eerst vaststellen hoe het nu werkt en presteert. Die nulmeting maakt latere vergelijking mogelijk. Een gewenste doelwaarde vastleggen hoort bij de volgende stap, niet bij de baseline.","hook":"Why improve? Link to the organizational direction.","prompt":"Which statement BEST distinguishes the improvement step 'What is the vision' from the improvement step 'Where are we now'?","options":["What is the vision? is concerned with the improvement-model step that links improvement to the organization's direction and objectives.; Where are we now? is concerned with the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline..","What is the vision? is concerned with the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline.; Where are we now? is concerned with the improvement-model step that links improvement to the organization's direction and objectives..","Both are primarily concerned with the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets.","Both are primarily concerned with the improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0281","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Where are we now?","why":"The decisive clue matches Where are we now?: The improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline. Where do we want to be? instead refers to the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets. Did we get there? instead refers to the improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target.","whyNl":"Eerst vaststellen hoe het nu werkt en presteert. Die nulmeting maakt latere vergelijking mogelijk. Een gewenste doelwaarde vastleggen hoort bij de volgende stap, niet bij de baseline. Vergelijk vooral met Where do we want to be?: Hier maak je de gewenste situatie concreet en meetbaar. Twee dagen doorlooptijd als doel is nog geen plan om die waarde te bereiken. Dat plan hoort bij How do we get there.","hook":"Now = baseline.","prompt":"Which statement BEST distinguishes the improvement step 'Where are we now' from the improvement step 'Where do we want to be'?","options":["Where are we now? is concerned with the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline.; Where do we want to be? is concerned with the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets..","Where are we now? is concerned with the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets.; Where do we want to be? is concerned with the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline..","Both are primarily concerned with the improvement-model step that compares actual results with the agreed target.","Both are primarily concerned with the improvement-model step that links improvement to the organization's direction and objectives."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0282","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Where do we want to be?","why":"The decisive clue matches Where do we want to be?: The improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets. Where are we now? instead refers to the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline. How do we get there? instead refers to the improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target.","whyNl":"Hier maak je de gewenste situatie concreet en meetbaar. Twee dagen doorlooptijd als doel is nog geen plan om die waarde te bereiken. Dat plan hoort bij How do we get there. Vergelijk vooral met Where are we now?: Eerst vaststellen hoe het nu werkt en presteert. Die nulmeting maakt latere vergelijking mogelijk. Een gewenste doelwaarde vastleggen hoort bij de volgende stap, niet bij de baseline.","hook":"Destination and measurable target.","prompt":"Which statement BEST distinguishes the improvement step 'Where do we want to be' from the improvement step 'Where are we now'?","options":["Where do we want to be? is concerned with the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets.; Where are we now? is concerned with the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline..","Where do we want to be? is concerned with the improvement-model step that establishes the current situation and a factual baseline.; Where are we now? is concerned with the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets..","Both are primarily concerned with the improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target.","Both are primarily concerned with the improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-71-0283","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"How do we get there?","why":"The decisive clue matches How do we get there?: The improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target. Where do we want to be? instead refers to the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets. Take action instead refers to the improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed.","whyNl":"Hier bepaal je de aanpak, acties, resources en volgorde. Het gewenste doel ligt al vast; je kiest nu de route. De acties daadwerkelijk uitvoeren hoort bij Take action. Vergelijk vooral met Where do we want to be?: Hier maak je de gewenste situatie concreet en meetbaar. Twee dagen doorlooptijd als doel is nog geen plan om die waarde te bereiken. Dat plan hoort bij How do we get there.","hook":"How = plan the route.","prompt":"Which statement BEST distinguishes the improvement step 'How do we get there' from the improvement step 'Where do we want to be'?","options":["How do we get there? is concerned with the improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target.; Where do we want to be? is concerned with the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets..","How do we get there? is concerned with the improvement-model step that defines the desired future state and measurable targets.; Where do we want to be? is concerned with the improvement-model step that develops the approach and actions needed to reach the target..","Both are primarily concerned with the improvement-model step in which the agreed improvement work is performed.","Both are primarily concerned with the improvement-model step that links improvement to the organization's direction and objectives."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"x701","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: vision","prompt":"An improvement team knows the current waiting time. Before selecting a target, it confirms how shorter waits support the organization's objectives. Which model step does that confirmation belong to?","options":["What is the vision?","Where are we now?","Where do we want to be?","How do we get there?"],"why":"Connecting the improvement to organizational direction belongs to the vision step, even if some baseline data already exists. A numeric future target belongs to \"Where do we want to be?\".","hook":"Vision: why this improvement matters to the organization.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De handeling verbindt de verbetering aan organisatiedoelen: What is the vision? Dat er al meetgegevens liggen verandert het doel van deze specifieke stap niet. Een meetbaar toekomsttarget is Where do we want to be?; concrete acties kiezen is How do we get there?","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x702","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: baseline","prompt":"A team documents the existing workflow, assesses available skills and measures current performance. Which continual improvement model step is this?","options":["Where are we now?","What is the vision?","Where do we want to be?","Did we get there?"],"why":"These activities assess the current state and establish a baseline. \"Did we get there?\" evaluates achieved results against the target after action has been taken.","hook":"Baseline first; achieved results later.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De bestaande situatie en mogelijkheden beoordelen is Where are we now? Het is een nulmeting. Did we get there? gebruikt ook cijfers, maar pas om na uitvoering resultaten met het doel te vergelijken. Het moment en het meetdoel zijn beslissend.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x703","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: target","prompt":"The current fulfilment time is five days. The team agrees that success means two days by the end of the quarter. Which step does agreeing this target represent?","options":["Where do we want to be?","What is the vision?","How do we get there?","Did we get there?"],"why":"A specific desired future state belongs to \"Where do we want to be?\". The improvement plan explains how to reach it; evaluating results checks whether it was reached.","hook":"The target is the destination, not the route.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Twee dagen aan het einde van het kwartaal is het gewenste meetbare eindpunt. Daarom Where do we want to be? Het vertelt nog niet hoe je daar komt. Het woord deadline maakt een target geen uitvoeringsplan; achteraf resultaat meten is weer een andere stap.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x704","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: plan","prompt":"The vision, baseline and measurable target have been agreed. The team chooses actions, resources and an order for carrying them out. Which step is it performing?","options":["How do we get there?","Where do we want to be?","Take action","How do we keep the momentum going?"],"why":"Choosing the route and arranging the work creates the improvement plan. Executing that plan is \"Take action\". Maintaining gains belongs to the momentum step.","hook":"Planning the work is different from doing the work.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Acties, middelen en volgorde kiezen beschrijft de route: How do we get there? Uitvoeren is Take action. Het target is al vastgesteld. Resultaat vasthouden hoort bij momentum en volgt op een bereikt en geëvalueerd resultaat.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x705","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: action","prompt":"An agreed improvement plan calls for a revised workflow. Staff now put the workflow into use and carry out the planned changes. Which model step is this?","options":["Take action","How do we get there?","Where do we want to be?","Did we get there?"],"why":"Implementing the plan is \"Take action\". Planning the changes and evaluating their achieved effects are separate steps, even though feedback can be used throughout.","hook":"The plan is now being carried out.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De afgesproken wijzigingen worden daadwerkelijk uitgevoerd: Take action. Ze bedenken en plannen is How do we get there? Beoordelen of het resultaat bereikt is, is Did we get there? Feedback kan overal helpen, maar die doelen blijven verschillend.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x706","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: evaluation","prompt":"After an improvement, the team compares measured results with the agreed target and determines whether the objective was achieved. Which step is this?","options":["Did we get there?","Where are we now?","Where do we want to be?","How do we keep the momentum going?"],"why":"Comparing achieved results with the intended target evaluates success. Measuring the initial baseline is \"Where are we now?\"; sustaining the result addresses momentum.","hook":"Compare the result with the destination you chose.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De gerealiseerde resultaten vergelijken met het afgesproken doel is Did we get there? De oorspronkelijke nulmeting is Where are we now? De gewenste toekomstige situatie vaststellen is Where do we want to be?; resultaat borgen is momentum.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x707","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement: momentum","prompt":"The target has been reached. A manager reinforces the new behavior, communicates the benefits and helps the team avoid returning to old methods. Which step is most directly illustrated?","options":["How do we keep the momentum going?","Did we get there?","Take action","What is the vision?"],"why":"These actions sustain and build on achieved improvements. Evaluating whether the target was reached has already happened; preserving the gains is the current emphasis.","hook":"Keep the gains from slipping away.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Het doel is al behaald. Nieuwe gewoonten ondersteunen en terugval voorkomen hoort bij How do we keep the momentum going? Nogmaals vaststellen of het target behaald is zou evaluatie zijn. De beschreven nadruk is behoud en verder bouwen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x708","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Continual improvement","prompt":"Which TWO statements about continual improvement are correct?\n1. Everyone should have responsibility for contributing to improvement.\n2. A dedicated improvement team takes all improvement responsibility away from other staff.\n3. Entering an idea in a register means it has been approved for implementation.\n4. Improvement ideas can be recorded and prioritized in a continual improvement register.","options":["1 and 4","1 and 2","2 and 3","3 and 4"],"why":"Everyone can contribute, with dedicated people providing support and coordination. A register helps manage opportunities; recording an idea is not the same as authorizing or implementing it.","hook":"Capture ideas, assess them, and keep responsibility shared.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"1 en 4 zijn juist. Iedereen kan bijdragen en een register ondersteunt vastleggen en prioriteren van kansen. Een apart team haalt verantwoordelijkheid niet weg bij de rest. Een idee registreren is geen toestemming om het direct uit te voeren.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"x709","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident management","prompt":"A workaround restores a failed service to normal operation. The cause is still unknown. Which statement best describes the situation?","options":["The incident can be resolved after restoration is confirmed, while cause investigation continues separately","The incident must remain unresolved until the underlying problem is permanently removed","The unknown cause means the workaround cannot count as service restoration","The incident becomes a service request once a workaround is available"],"why":"Incident management focuses on confirmed service restoration and can resolve an incident without removing its underlying cause. Problem management can continue investigating; appropriate confirmation and closure procedures still apply.","hook":"Restore the service; investigate the cause through problem management.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Na bevestigd serviceherstel kan het incident opgelost worden volgens de geldende procedure. Problem management kan de oorzaak verder onderzoeken. Een workaround bewijst geen definitieve oplossing, maar het ontbreken van root cause blokkeert niet automatisch incidentherstel.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x710","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident prioritization","prompt":"Incident A affects a payroll deadline due in one hour. Incident B has more reports but affects a non-critical feature with an agreed workaround. What should guide their priority?","options":["Business impact and urgency, using the agreed prioritization approach","The total number of reports, because that establishes the resolution order","The order in which the first report for each incident was received","The estimated technical effort, with the quickest restoration attempted first"],"why":"Priority should reflect business impact and urgency. Report count, arrival order and repair effort can provide context but do not by themselves establish business priority.","hook":"Priority asks how much it matters and how soon action is needed.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Impact op de business en urgentie bepalen prioriteit volgens afspraken. Meer meldingen betekent niet automatisch hogere prioriteit. Aankomstvolgorde of technische oplostijd kan context geven, maar mag de gevolgen van een kritieke deadline niet vervangen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x711","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Incident management","prompt":"A service desk cannot restore an incident using its available knowledge. Which response best supports incident management?","options":["Involve suitable specialists while maintaining coordination and communication","Retain ownership within the first team until it identifies the cause","Resolve the incident record when a specialist accepts the handover","Delay restoration while a separate team completes cause analysis"],"why":"Incident management can draw on different teams and suppliers to restore service. Escalating to expertise does not remove the need for coordination or keeping users informed.","hook":"Bring in expertise without losing coordination.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Gebruik passende expertise en houd herstel en communicatie gecoördineerd. Het incident hoeft niet bij het eerste team te blijven tot de oorzaak bekend is. Alleen overdragen of anders classificeren is geen serviceherstel. Gebruikers blijven tijdige informatie nodig hebben.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x712","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Problem management","prompt":"Trend analysis identifies a component likely to cause future service interruptions, although it has not yet caused one. How does this relate to problem management?","options":["Problem management can investigate a potential cause before an incident occurs","A problem can be recorded only after the first associated incident is resolved","The potential cause is already a known error because it has been detected","The potential cause should be treated as an incident regardless of service impact"],"why":"Problems include potential causes of incidents, so identification can be proactive. Detection alone does not establish an analysed known error, and a potential future interruption is not itself an incident.","hook":"Problem management can act before the first disruption.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een problem kan een potentiële oorzaak zijn, dus onderzoek mag vóór het eerste incident plaatsvinden. Alleen een risico of defect opmerken is nog geen analyse voor known error. Zonder actuele serviceverstoring is het evenmin automatisch een incident.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x713","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Known errors and workarounds","prompt":"A problem has been analysed and remains unresolved. No effective workaround has been found. Which statement is correct?","options":["It can still be a known error; a workaround is not a prerequisite for that definition","It becomes a known error only when a workaround is documented","It remains an incident until an effective workaround restores service","It must be recorded as a change because the analysis is complete"],"why":"The known error definition requires an analysed, unresolved problem. A workaround may reduce its effects, but its absence does not stop the problem from being a known error.","hook":"Analysed and unresolved is enough for a known error.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Analyse plus nog onopgelost maakt dit een known error. Een effectieve workaround is geen voorwaarde. Het blijft niet uitsluitend een incident tot iemand een omweg heeft. Een change kan later nodig zijn voor de oplossing, maar is niet hetzelfde als het problem.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x714","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Problem management","prompt":"A permanent fix would cost much more than the expected benefit. An effective workaround keeps the remaining impact acceptable. Which approach best fits problem management?","options":["Assess and manage the residual risk, keeping the known error and workaround under review","Treat the problem as permanently resolved because the workaround is effective","Require a permanent fix before any related incidents can be resolved","Stop reviewing the known error once its workaround has been documented"],"why":"Problem management balances costs, risks and benefits; not every problem receives an immediate permanent fix. An accepted workaround does not remove the need to manage the unresolved issue.","hook":"Managed risk may be preferable to an unjustified fix.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Afwegen van kosten, risico en baten kan betekenen dat een permanente fix wordt uitgesteld. Blijf het resterende risico en de workaround beheren. Een effectieve omweg maakt de oorzaak niet permanent opgelost en is geen reden om alle beoordeling te stoppen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x715","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Standard changes","prompt":"A low-risk installation follows a well-understood, fully documented and pre-authorized procedure. Which statement is correct?","options":["It can be a standard change when carried out within the authorized conditions","It is a normal change because each execution needs a new authorization","It is an emergency change because a separate approval step is unnecessary","It is outside change enablement because the installation is routine"],"why":"A standard change is low risk, well understood, documented and pre-authorized. The authorization applies to the defined procedure and conditions, not to arbitrary variations.","hook":"Standard means pre-authorized within a defined scope.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Standard change geldt binnen de bekende, gedocumenteerde en vooraf geautoriseerde voorwaarden. Routine betekent niet buiten change enablement. Voor een afwijkende uitvoering kan nieuwe autorisatie nodig zijn. Spoed en geen losse goedkeuringsstap zijn niet hetzelfde.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x716","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Emergency changes","prompt":"An urgent security patch is needed to address a serious vulnerability. What is appropriate for an emergency change?","options":["Use an accelerated assessment and authorization path appropriate to the urgency","Use the standard change path because urgent work is automatically pre-authorized","Deploy first in every case, then obtain retrospective authorization as the normal rule","Use the normal lead time even when the delay would leave unacceptable exposure"],"why":"Emergency changes need expedited handling, with assessment and authorization adapted to urgency. Emergency status does not itself mean pre-authorization or the absence of controls.","hook":"Urgency changes the speed and path, not the need for control.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een emergency change krijgt passende versnelde beoordeling en autorisatie. Urgentie betekent niet automatisch vooraf geautoriseerd, ongecontroleerd uitvoeren of altijd achteraf goedkeuren. De normale doorlooptijd blind vasthouden kan de resterende blootstelling vergroten.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x717","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change authority","prompt":"Two changes have different risks and potential impacts. How should their change authorities be selected?","options":["Use the appropriate authority for each type and level of risk","Send every change to the same senior committee to ensure consistency","Give the implementing technician authority for every change they perform","Use the same authority whenever changes are scheduled for the same day"],"why":"An appropriate authority should be assigned to the type of change and its risk. This can be an individual or group; a single committee need not authorize every change.","hook":"Match the authority to the change.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De change authority hoort te passen bij type en risico. Dat kan een persoon of groep zijn. Eén commissie hoeft niet alles te autoriseren; een uitvoerder is ook niet automatisch voor iedere eigen wijziging bevoegd. De kalenderdatum bepaalt het risico niet.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x718","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Change schedule","prompt":"Two independently approved changes affect the same service during the same maintenance window. What is the main value of the change schedule here?","options":["Making the overlap visible so the changes can be coordinated and conflicts managed","Providing authorization that replaces the approvals already given for the changes","Showing that each change has met all technical acceptance criteria","Converting both changes into standard changes because their timing is known"],"why":"A change schedule helps coordinate work, communicate plans and identify conflicts. Being on the schedule does not replace authorization or prove successful testing.","hook":"A schedule coordinates; it does not authorize by itself.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De change schedule toont planning, mogelijke botsingen en afhankelijkheden. Afstemmen blijft nodig wanneer wijzigingen afzonderlijk al zijn goedgekeurd. Een kalenderitem geeft geen extra autorisatie, bewijst geen geslaagde tests en maakt een change niet standaard.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x719","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service request management","prompt":"A user requests access under an agreed request model, but the model requires a manager's approval. Which handling is appropriate?","options":["Follow the predefined request workflow, including the required approval","Treat it as an incident because access has not yet been granted","Skip the approval because all service requests are pre-authorized changes","Start a problem investigation because the user cannot currently perform the activity"],"why":"Service requests are agreed normal service actions, but their workflows can still include approvals and security checks. A request is not automatically an incident or a pre-authorized change.","hook":"Normal request does not mean no approval.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een vooraf afgesproken request kan gewoon een goedkeuringsstap bevatten. Volg het model. Nog geen nieuw recht hebben is niet automatisch een incident. Routineverzoeken zijn niet allemaal pre-authorized changes en een mogelijke vertraging is niet vanzelf een problem.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x720","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service request management","prompt":"A user asks for an agreed standard software installation. The request workflow includes a pre-authorized change. Which statement is most accurate?","options":["Request management handles fulfilment, while the change follows its authorized change model","The request must be reclassified as an incident because installation changes the service","Request management replaces change enablement whenever a user initiates the work","The standard change must become a normal change each time a user requests it"],"why":"Practices can work together. A service request can include a standard change without losing its request workflow or bypassing the conditions of pre-authorization.","hook":"One request can draw on more than one practice.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een service request kan een standard change bevatten. Request management coördineert de afhandeling en het change-model blijft gelden. De practices vervangen elkaar niet. Het verzoek maakt de change niet automatisch normal of het ticket een incident.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x721","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service desk","prompt":"Routine requests increasingly use self-service. Which capability becomes particularly valuable for the service desk's remaining interactions?","options":["Understanding users and business context, with effective communication and empathy","Measuring success mainly by reducing the duration of every conversation","Taking over every specialist team's technical resolution responsibilities","Requiring users to identify the correct technical team before making contact"],"why":"Automation can leave more complex or sensitive interactions for people. Communication, empathy and business understanding remain essential; the desk need not personally solve every specialist issue.","hook":"Automation increases the importance of the human interaction.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Door automatisering blijven vaak complexere menselijke contacten over. Begrip van de gebruiker, empathie en communicatie blijven daarom belangrijk. De desk hoeft niet elke specialistische oplossing zelf te leveren. Gespreksduur verkorten is geen doel los van goede hulp.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x722","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service desk","prompt":"A service desk operates from several locations but should act as one coherent contact point. Which arrangement best supports this?","options":["Shared information and tools, with coordinated ways of working and communication","Independent local records, with users responsible for carrying information between desks","A rule that incidents can be handled only at the location where they were reported","Optimize each local queue without coordinating the overall user experience"],"why":"A virtual or distributed desk can provide coherent support through shared tools, information and working practices. Physical co-location is not the defining requirement.","hook":"One experience can come from several locations.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een verdeelde desk kan één contactpunt vormen met gedeelde informatie, tools en gecoördineerde werkwijzen. Fysiek bij elkaar zitten is niet vereist. Gebruikers telkens opnieuw informatie laten overdragen of cases aan één locatie vastzetten maakt de ondersteuning minder samenhangend.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x723","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service level management","prompt":"Individual infrastructure targets are met, but customers cannot complete transactions quickly enough. Which response best supports service level management?","options":["Review end-to-end service targets and actual customer experience","Report success because the component targets have all been achieved","Average the component scores to obtain the customer's service experience","Replace customer feedback with more detailed measurements of each component"],"why":"Service targets should reflect business outcomes and the overall experience. Good component results can coexist with poor end-to-end service, so component metrics alone are insufficient.","hook":"Green components can still add up to a poor service.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Groene infrastructuurtargets bewijzen geen goede end-to-end service. Bekijk het echte businessresultaat, de gebruikerservaring en de gekozen targets. Meer componentmetingen of succes rapporteren op basis van losse onderdelen lost de slechte transactieservice niet op.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x724","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service level management","prompt":"Which TWO inputs together provide a useful basis for understanding service performance?\n1. The provider's assumptions without checking with consumers.\n2. Customer and user discussions about their experience.\n3. Measured service results.\n4. Component availability treated as a complete substitute for service experience.","options":["2 and 3","1 and 2","3 and 4","1 and 4"],"why":"Quantitative measures and qualitative discussions complement each other. Assumptions and isolated component metrics cannot fully establish whether the service meets consumer needs.","hook":"Combine numbers with conversations.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"2 en 3 zijn juist: gesprekken met klanten en gebruikers en gemeten serviceresultaten vullen elkaar aan. Provider-aannames zonder controle zijn onvoldoende. Losse componentbeschikbaarheid is geen volledige vervanging voor de echte service-ervaring.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"x725","criterion":"7.1","lo":7,"tag":"Service level management","prompt":"A provider and customer are drafting an SLA. Which approach best supports meaningful service level management?","options":["Agree clear service targets that relate to business needs and can be understood by both parties","List every internal technical measure and treat that list as the service commitment","Base commitments on what is easiest to measure before discussing customer outcomes","Let each technical team define its own commitments without checking the overall service"],"why":"SLAs should express agreed service expectations in a clear, business-relevant way. Internal technical detail can support delivery, but is not a substitute for meaningful service commitments.","hook":"An SLA should describe service quality that the customer can recognize.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een SLA bevat duidelijke, gezamenlijk begrijpelijke targets die bij businessbehoeften passen. Niet alles wat intern meetbaar is, is een zinvolle servicebelofte. Bespreek eerst relevante outcomes; laat lokale teamtargets niet het beeld van de hele service vervangen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"}]);
